# Advisories that govulncheck reports as called and that this chain accepts, one per line:
#     <ID> <reason, mandatory, at least 40 characters: the executable path and why it is acceptable>
# Read by scripts/govulncheck_filter.py through `make govulncheck`. A called advisory that is not
# listed here stays red; an entry whose advisory is no longer reported at all is refused, so a
# line here cannot outlive the thing it excuses. Accepting an advisory that has a fixed version is
# the wrong fix: bump the dependency instead. The filter prints the entry points the scanner
# traces for every accepted advisory, so a path that changes is visible at the next run.
